S.No,Questions,Yes,No,Not Applicable,Comment,Date
1,Confirm nature of business and accounting method,,,,,
2,Check bank reconciliation reports for any differences.,,,,,
3,Check trade creditors and debtors summary report if there is any overpaid customer or supplier.,,,,,
4,"Trade creditors should not have any contact of director or cash suppliers like (Amazon, Tesco, Ebay, Co Op etc.)",,,,,
5,Compare monthly profit and loss figures,,,,,
6,Always run the detailed account transaction report for the current period and of last period as well to confirm the previous practices.,,,,,
7,Check the particular supplier or customer are in a single code and same type of expense is not been kept into different codes and the VAT treatment on them.,,,,,
8,"Make sure to check the VAT treatment for the tax sensitive account heads. i.e. (Bank charges, insurance, rates, rent, PPS etc.)",,,,,
9,The payroll liability should be correctly posted and the payment has been posted in the correct account heads with No VAT.,,,,,
10,The PAYE liability should match with the P32,,,,,
